   "limitation": "The five-chamber plane cannot both contain the heart's long axis and pass through the aortic valve - the valve sits about 23 degrees off the long-axis plane. So this view is a genuine anterior TILT rather than a rotation, and it buys the aorta at the cost of the tricuspid valve, which drops out of plane. The RV outflow tract appears at the anterior edge."
